comment.body:
**Simplification: `goal_marker` is total now, so wrapping its result in `Some(...)` just to unwrap it twice below is redundant state.**

The `Option` existed because the old `goal_marker(content : String) -> GoalMarker?` could fail to parse. It cannot fail any more. This reads more directly as a single match on the item:

```suggestion
  let goal_marker : @transcript.GoalMarker? = match item {
    @protocol.Goal(change) => Some(@transcript.goal_marker(change))
    _ => None
  }
```

…or better, collapse `goal`, `goal_marker` and the `goal_pending` test into one `match item { @protocol.Goal(change) => { … } _ => self }` arm, which removes both `is Some(marker)` re-tests.

The comment just above ("A `[goal]` marker commit…") should lose the literal marker text too — the commit is a typed `Goal` item now.

